      "problem": "Solve for $w$ where $\\frac{w-3}{7}=\\frac{1-2w}{6}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we cross-multiply:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{w-3}{7} & =\\frac{1-2w}{6} \\\\ (w-3)\\cdot 6 & =7\\cdot (1-2w)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we proceed as usual to solve the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(w-3)\\cdot 6 & =7\\cdot (1-2w) \\\\ 6w-18 & =7-14w \\\\ 6w-18+14w & =7-14w+14w \\\\ 20w-18 & =7 \\\\ 20w-18+18 & =7+18 \\\\ 20w & =25 \\\\ \\frac{20w}{20} & =\\frac{25}{20} \\\\ w & =\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
